# FinanceFlow MVP - Environment Configuration Template
# ==================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your credentials
#
# IMPORTANT: This app works in TWO MODES:
#
# 1. MOCK MODE (Default - No setup required)
#    - Just run `npm run dev` and login with any credentials
#    - Perfect for testing UI/UX and development
#
# 2. REAL MODE (Requires setup below)
#    - Full PDF upload, AI extraction, and database features
#    - Requires Supabase and OpenAI accounts
#
# ==================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE CONFIGURATION (Required for Real Mode)
# ------------------------------------------------------
# Get these from: https://app.supabase.com
# 1. Create a new project (takes ~2 minutes)
# 2. Go to Settings > API
# 3. Copy the values below:

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# ------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI CONFIGURATION (Required for Real Mode)
# ------------------------------------------------------
# Get your API key from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# 1. Sign up for OpenAI account
# 2. Create a new API key
# 3. Paste it below (starts with 'sk-'):

OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-api-key-here

# ------------------------------------------------------
# APPLICATION URL (Optional)
# ------------------------------------------------------
# Default: http://localhost:3000
# Only change if running on different port or domain

NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ==================================================
# SETUP STEPS FOR REAL MODE:
# ==================================================
#
# 1. Create Supabase Project:
#    - Visit https://supabase.com and sign up
#    - Create new project and wait for provisioning
#    - Copy credentials from Settings > API
#
# 2. Setup Database:
#    - In Supabase, go to SQL Editor
#    - Open the file `supabase-setup.sql` from this project
#    - Copy and paste the entire SQL script
#    - Click "Run" to create tables and storage
#
# 3. Get OpenAI API Key:
#    - Visit https://platform.openai.com
#    - Create account and add payment method
#    - Generate new API key
#    - Copy the key (you'll only see it once!)
#
# 4. Configure this file:
#    - Copy this template to `.env.local`:
#      cp .env.local.template .env.local
#    - Fill in all the values above
#    - Save the file
#
# 5. Restart dev server:
#    npm run dev
#
# 6. Test real mode:
#    - Go to http://localhost:3000/upload
#    - Upload an electricity bill PDF
#    - Watch it process in real-time!
#
# ==================================================
# COST ESTIMATES (Real Mode):
# ==================================================
#
# Supabase (Free Tier):
#   - 500MB database storage
#   - 1GB file storage
#   - 2GB bandwidth/month
#   - Perfect for testing and MVP
#
# OpenAI (Pay as you go):
#   - ~$0.002 per PDF document processed
#   - 100 documents ≈ $0.20
#   - Uses gpt-4o-mini (cheapest, fastest)
#
# ==================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING:
# ==================================================
#
# Issue: "Missing Supabase environment variables"
# Solution: Make sure this file is named `.env.local` (not .env.local.template)
#
# Issue: "Failed to fetch document"
# Solution: Check that you ran supabase-setup.sql in your Supabase SQL Editor
#
# Issue: "OpenAI API error"
# Solution: Verify your API key is correct and has billing enabled
#
# Issue: App still uses mock data
# Solution: Restart the dev server after adding credentials
#
# ==================================================
